      "index": 7,
      "rootCommentId": null,
      "threadId": null,
      "path": null,
      "line": null,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "## Automated Code Review — REQUEST_CHANGES\n\n**Summary**: Two blocking issues: the `CRAP + duplication` CI gate is red (`ApprovalCommands._onMessageUpdate` grew to CC 16; the pinned 12.0 ratchet fails even at 100% coverage), and the new E8 width seam loses its `onResized` hook on the first model `copyWith` swap, so mid-run resizes are never tracked in production (the new UT drives the boot model, a path production never takes). Otherwise a well-tested change — the full AC/E matrix (AC1–AC7, AC9, E1–E4) is pinned by 29 green tests plus 20 bench parser tests, and AC6 stdout purity is backed by the real `HepEventsIO` host wiring.\n\n**Key Issues**:\n- 🚨 CI red: split `_onMessageUpdate` (CC 10 → 16) — unfixable by tests, CRAP ≥ CC at full coverage\n- 🚨 E8: `FaTuiModel.copyWith` drops `onResized` → hook fires only for the startup resize\n- ⚠️ Multi-tool-call narration flushes after the first result row (position drift)\n- 💡 Card wrap budget starves the `log:` path; literal ESC byte in the Python fixture; redaction now touches interactive deltas (doc nuance)\n\n**Next Steps**:\n1. Split `_onMessageUpdate` into tool-gate / text / thinking helpers (repo precedent: `_flushAssistantStreamAtEnd`)\n2. Re-attach `onResized` in `copyWith` and pin the production swap path in the test\n3. Non-blocking, for the follow-up card: the ticket's IT-TUI pty harness, IT-TUI-IMG image fixtures and the pty-less E2E were not delivered — the E8 swap-path bug is exactly the class of gap they would catch; the PR description's bench verify command should read `cd bench/terminal_bench && python3 -m unittest test_bench_metrics` (`cd bench` fails with ModuleNotFoundError)"
    }
  ]
}

